.\" Title: vrl-config-check
.\" Author: vrl contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\"
.TH VRL\-CONFIG\-CHECK 1 "2025" "vrl" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrl\-config\-check \- validate configuration files without starting

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrl
\fBconfig\-check\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICONFIG\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Validate vrl configuration files without starting an instance. Checks all configuration files in the standard load order (user config \fB~/.config/vrl/config.yaml\fR or \fBconfig.toml\fR, then local \fB./vrl.yaml\fR or \fBvrl.toml\fR) and reports any errors or warnings.

Configuration validation checks include: valid field types, value ranges (e.g., rows 1\-200, cols 1\-500), required fields, conflicting options, and deprecated settings.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to a specific configuration file to validate. When omitted, the standard config file locations are checked.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Validate default configuration files:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrl config\-check\fR
Configuration OK: ~/.config/vrl/config.yaml
.fi
.RE

.PP
Validate a specific config file:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrl config\-check \-c /path/to/custom.yaml\fR
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Configuration is valid (no errors).

.TP
.B 1
Configuration has errors. Warning messages may also be shown but do not cause a non-zero exit.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vrl (1)
